Lily Ray's URL: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/another-way-youre-being-lied-geo-ai-search-lily-ray-t8shf/

As an SEO agency team with mid-size to enterprise clients, it would be easy to position ourselves as AEO/GEO “experts” by taking credit for the visibility that many clients have enjoyed in LLM responses since the day LLMs became available to the public.

There is a reason we don’t.

The truth is, many brands automatically earned brand mentions and citations in LLMs by - wait for it - being among the best and most frequently cited brands in the space.

That “knowledge” was already reflected in their training data.

We have some clients who had already driven millions in revenue from AI search by H2 of 2025. What did they do differently for GEO? (Aside from the work we have been doing with SEO for years, plus all the other integrated marketing approaches they have implemented to become well-known and trusted brands?) The true answer: nothing.

We have numerous clients who are consistently among the top cited companies when you ask different LLMs about the best brands in their industry. What did they do differently for GEO to earn those mentions? Literally nothing. They are just often seen - by society, and by extension, the internet & AI - as the top brands in the space.

Let’s use the Levi’s example I recently shared using Profound data: they own the highest AI search share of voice across all LLMs for prompts related to jeans. Is it because of GEO? Nah. It’s because they are Levi’s.

Many clients have also seen substantial visibility and citations in Google’s AI Overviews and AI Mode this year, with the same content we have optimized for years for organic search. In many cases, nothing new or special was done “for AI” to earn those positions. This is why Google is literally on record saying “good SEO is good GEO” and that - wait for it - you “don’t have to do anything different for inclusion in AIO/AI Mode.”

Now - to be clear - I absolutely DO believe you can do work to drive additional visibility and citations in AI Search. This is why we do offer a new AEO service at Amsive, and I stand behind the work we are providing for clients on that front. Initial feedback from AEO clients is that they are finding these deliverables quite helpful. We are using a variety of new tools and methodologies to analyze and explain the lay of the land in AI search, and to find relevant opportunities to drive even more visibility and citations where it matters, across the AI search landscape.

But I think it’s important for those in our industry (and the new GEO folks who just got here) to be transparent and honest that many brands mentioned in AI search appear as such simply because it’s a reflection of the (often 1 year+ old) training data used to train the LLMs that generate their names. Not because of GEO magic.

Again, I share stuff like this frequently, because frankly, too many people are being lied to right now and promised the moon. Just today, I was served 5 (!) Instagram ads by brand new companies claiming they have the secret recipe to unlocking guaranteed AI search visibility, and that your brand will be invisible without it. 😩 

Please don't fall for this snake oil.

As with all things in Search - be cautious of companies guaranteeing anything. Ask for evidence that their work is the thing that moved the needle - not that the LLM would have answered that same way, with or without them.

